Backpropagation is the core of the modern neural network. 
backpropagation:
  backpropagation is basically a chain of rule, applied backwards to compute how much each parameter is contributing to the error.
  it efficiently evaluates the gradient of loss function, wrt to weights of a neural network. 
  This allows us to iteratively tune the weights of neural network to minimize the loss function, there by improving the accuracy of the loss function.


Forward Pass:
  Simply take the inputs, pass through the model, compute output and loss, with no learning. 

|Forward Pass | Backward Pass|
------------------------------
|Compute Outputs| Compute Gradients|
|Input -> Loss | Loss -> Parameters|
|Use current weights|Update Weights|
|No learning yet|learning happens|

Backpropagation go through the expression graph, recursively apply chain rule from calculus, this allows us to do derivate of g wrt to all internal nodes, inputs. 
then we will be in a position to calculate/query grad, wrt to each parameter. with that, we will be knowing, how input parameters are effecting the output.

derivate of output wrt to input parameter tells the slope, if we nudge the parameter, then it is going to change by slope.
